<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		An explicit file, because generation produces the wrong shape here.

		`INFOPLIST_KEY_NSExtensionPointIdentifier` writes a *top-level*
		`NSExtensionPointIdentifier`, and an app extension needs it nested
		inside an `NSExtension` dictionary. installd rejects the bundle:

		    extensionDictionary must be set in placeholder attributes for an
		    app extension placeholder

		so AtticWidget.appex could not be installed at all, which takes the
		whole app down with it — the extension is embedded in TimeCapsule.app.
		Nine audit rounds missed this because CI only ever compiled the app;
		the first run that actually installed it failed in under three
		minutes.

		`GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE` stays on, so the display name and the photo
		library usage description are still merged in from build settings.
		Only the part generation gets wrong lives here.
	-->
	<key>NSExtension</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSExtensionPointIdentifier</key>
		<string>com.apple.widgetkit-extension</string>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
